W = p0 + [-1/200,1/200]^2,  q_n = p0 + (2^(-n-3)/100, 0)
  n=0: max|z-q_n| <= 2001/250000 = 0.008004   (need < 1-eps)
  n=1: max|z-q_n| <= 3763/500000 = 0.007526   (need < 1-eps)
  n=2: max|z-q_n| <= 114/15625 = 0.007296   (need < 1-eps)
  n=3: max|z-q_n| <= 7183/1000000 = 0.007183   (need < 1-eps)
  n=4: max|z-q_n| <= 7127/1000000 = 0.007127   (need < 1-eps)
  n=5: max|z-q_n| <= 7099/1000000 = 0.007099   (need < 1-eps)
  n=6: max|z-q_n| <= 1417/200000 = 0.007085   (need < 1-eps)
  n=7: max|z-q_n| <= 3539/500000 = 0.007078   (need < 1-eps)

=> W is contained in B(q_n, 1/2) for every n, so 'agree off B(q_n, 1-eps)'
   with eps = 1/2 holds for the pair (m3 colouring, background c0).

sampled points satisfy |y + r u - q_n| >= r - |y-q_n| > 1 - eps = 0.5
and                                 <= r + |y-q_n| < 1 + eps = 1.5
distance from p0:  |y+r u - p0| in ( 1-eps-|q_n-p0| , 1+eps+|q_n-p0| )
  n=0: annulus (0.498750, 1.501250)  contains the m3 annulus A = (1-71/10000, 1+71/10000)
  n=1: annulus (0.499375, 1.500625)  contains the m3 annulus A = (1-71/10000, 1+71/10000)
  n=2: annulus (0.499688, 1.500312)  contains the m3 annulus A = (1-71/10000, 1+71/10000)

m3's exact certificate: A = {1-71/10000 <= |q-p0| <= 1+71/10000} meets no hexagon of c0-colour 0, 2 or 3.
Hence every label in the palette P_{q_n}(e) lies in {1,4,5,6}, while c(q_n) in {0,2,3}:
the cyclic centre's own colour is outside its palette, as required (paper Lemma D), and
the palette sees only the BACKGROUND. Decoupling is what makes the k>=7 counterexample run.
